# SwiftFormat.
#
# Formatting is not worth arguing about, so it is not argued about: this file decides, and
# `swiftformat .` applies it. What matters is that the rules match the three other frontends'
# Prettier configuration wherever the languages allow — a reader moving between the React, Angular
# and Swift versions of the same screen should see the same shape.
#
#     brew install swiftformat
#     swiftformat .

--swiftversion 5.10

--indent 4
--maxwidth 110
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--wrapcollections preserve
--closingparen balanced
--commas always
--trimwhitespace always
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--self remove
--importgrouping testable-bottom
--funcattributes prev-line
--typeattributes prev-line

# Disabled with reasons:
#
# blankLinesAroundMark  — the MARK comments in this codebase separate sections that already have
#                         blank lines around them; the rule fights the doc comments above them.
# redundantType         — `let x: ViewState<Catalogue> = .idle` reads better than `= ViewState.idle`
#                         and the explicit type is the documentation.
# wrapMultilineStatementBraces — reformats every SwiftUI modifier chain for no gain.
--disable blankLinesAroundMark, redundantType, wrapMultilineStatementBraces

--exclude Pizza.xcodeproj,DerivedData,.build
